{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/273871-cma-saint-of-the-abyss-style","id":273871,"title":"[CMA]Saint of the Abyss Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-06T08:37:47-07:00","id":273871,"title":"[CMA]Saint of the Abyss Style","content":"<span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PkCxx73lPtNHPy-PtztZ3JYYzl_CQ8qPBo1WxKUYNps/edit\" target=\"_blank\">I tried to get the formatting right and c/p it here, but, you know, screw it.</a> </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T11:35:38-07:00","id":274066,"title":"","content":"This is beautiful. I'm still getting used to the mechanics, so I can't critique you there, but this seems like it'd make a good fit for Western Lunars(as mentioned), Deathknights, and Kimbery favoring Infernals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T13:14:38-07:00","id":274129,"title":"","content":"Nice style, certainly something that Western Lunars can use... Or Siakal Exigents.<ul><li>The Abyss Opens: Nice and gets around the tick six pileup problem that usually occurs.</li> <li>Typhoon-And-Whirlpool Dance: I assume you mean 5 motes. Secondly when you say successes, do these successes apply to challenges based on moving around in the environment or do they translate to additional movement speed as well? I assume this would be the charm to allow one to swim through water or liquid mediums without penalty correct?</li> <li>Dark Dwelling Hellsquid Mantle: What if someone attempts to blow away the cloud? The Fog Generator charm for Alchemicals has rules like this, and probably one of the first things I'd imagine a PC would do is to try and blow this cloud away, so some rulings on that would be nice.</li> <li>Terrible Grandgousier Swallow-Strike: May want to mention that a person needs to use their hands or something in order to grip someone and not a spear. I think it's fine to do something like a spear poke then grab them, provided they use a hand to do so.</li> <li>Ten Thousand Open Arms: Do I need to Flurry my clinch control rolls? Would I need to flurry any other action in addition to my clinch control roll?</li> <li>Armors-To-Tincan Depths Pressure: And if the armour itself has all of it's mobility and fatigue penalties nullified by charms or some sort? Such as the Alchemical Integration Aegis?</li> </ul><br /> Overall very well done, I like it. One of my players will probably love this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:38:18-07:00","id":274209,"title":"","content":"Was expecting Wolf Knight / Abysswalker Artorias Style. But not disappointed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T17:00:37-07:00","id":274273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/273871-cma-saint-of-the-abyss-style?p=274129#post274129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Typhoon-And-Whirlpool Dance: I assume you mean 5 motes. Secondly when you say successes, do these successes apply to challenges based on moving around in the environment or do they translate to additional movement speed as well? I assume this would be the charm to allow one to swim through water or liquid mediums without penalty correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're successes that add to all rolls made in order to or pertaining to moving around. So, chase rolls, jumping, keeping your balance, that kind of thing. And yes, this will cancel any penalty that would arise from moving in water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Dark Dwelling Hellsquid Mantle: What if someone attempts to blow away the cloud? The Fog Generator charm for Alchemicals has rules like this, and probably one of the first things I'd imagine a PC would do is to try and blow this cloud away, so some rulings on that would be nice. </div> </div> </div>The cloud has no material component, it is simply dark Essence; you can no more blow it away than you could blow away the kaleidoscopic aura of a Crystal Chameleon Stylist.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Terrible Grandgousier Swallow-Strike: May want to mention that a person needs to use their hands or something in order to grip someone and not a spear. I think it's fine to do something like a spear poke then grab them, provided they use a hand to do so. </div> </div> </div>Done.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Ten Thousand Open Arms: Do I need to Flurry my clinch control rolls? Would I need to flurry any other action in addition to my clinch control roll? </div> </div> </div>No, they happen reflexively. Edited.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Armors-To-Tincan Depths Pressure: And if the armour itself has all of it's mobility and fatigue penalties nullified by charms or some sort? Such as the Alchemical Integration Aegis? </div> </div> </div>If you can ignore fatigue and mobility penalties, you will suffer no ill effects from this CHarm, much as a Charm increasing wound penalties would have no effect on someone who negates them in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overall very well done, I like it. One of my players will probably love this. </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Having this style see actual use would be the best reward for writing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was expecting Wolf Knight / Abysswalker Artorias Style. But not disappointed. </div> </div> </div>I wish my computer could run Dark Souls without lagging like hell, then I could have fought Artorias too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}